# CampusNav - Campus Route Finder (CLI)

Finds the shortest walking route between places on the FAST-NUCES Karachi campus.
The campus is a weighted graph; routes come from Dijkstra's algorithm and are drawn
and colored in the terminal.

Features: shortest route, multi-stop route (A -> B -> C ...), nearest facility.

Data structures are written by hand (no std::vector / map / priority_queue / stack / queue):
hash table, stack, adjacency-list graph and min-heap.

## Build and run
    g++ -std=c++17 -O2 campus_map.cpp -o campus_map
    ./campus_map

Use a terminal at least 105 columns wide (UTF-8 and ANSI colors).

